DECATUR, GA — On Wednesday, April 7, Congressman Hank Johnson (GA-04) is holding a virtual "Teach-In" event to lift up the life-saving resources contained in the American Rescue Plan. The Teach-In will help people understand how they can benefit from the various provisions of the bill – connecting constituents with resources.

REGISTER HERE

Congressman Johnson will bring together experts from Small Business Administration (SBA), Internal Revenue Service (IRS), The Urban League of Atlanta, Atlanta Legal Aid, Department of Health and Human Services (HHS), Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA), Emory University, the Atlanta Food Bank and other experts to speak with Fourth District residents about what the American Rescue plan means for them, their families and small businesses – and how the ARP has empowered these agencies to help constituents. This event will be about an hour and a half with most time for Q&A.

WHO: Rep. Hank Johnson (GA-04); representatives from SBA, IRS, HHS, FEMA, Urban League, Atlanta Legal Aid, Atlanta Food Bank, and more;

WHAT: Virtual "Teach-In" on the American Rescue Plan via Zoom and on Facebook Live;

WHEN: Wednesday, April 7 from 3-4:30 PM;

WHERE: To register on Zoom: https://bit.ly/2R1ibJV or watch on Congressman Johnson's Facebook page: https://www.facebook.com/RepHankJohnson/. Or dial in: US: +1 669 254 5252 or +1 551 285 1373.

